The Skimmed CFG algorithm implemented here is a port of that project. The
following files contain code derived from the upstream work:

  sd_webui_skimmed_cfg/core.py

Specifically, get_skimming_mask() and skimmed_CFG() are ported verbatim, and
the bodies of all four modes follow the corresponding upstream nodes without
algorithmic change:

  Single Scale         <- CFG_Skimming_Single_Scale_Pre_CFG
  Replace              <- SkimReplacePreCFG
  Linear Interpolation <- SkimmedCFG_LinInterp_CFG_PreCFG
  Dual Scales          <- SkimmedCFG_LinInterp_DualScales_CFG_PreCFG

This includes the three sign-agreement conditions that build the skimming
mask, the flipping-filter branch, the sigma gating on Single Scale, the use
of (cond_scale - 1) on the Single Scale cond pass and on the second Replace
mask, the fallback_weight computations, the division-by-zero guard at
cond_scale <= 1 and the order in which the negative and positive weights are
applied in Dual Scales.


MODIFICATIONS
=============

The following changes were made to the upstream work in the course of
porting it to Forge-derived Stable Diffusion WebUIs. None of them alter the
algorithm itself.

  * Ported from ComfyUI node classes to a WebUI Script extension. The node
    schemas are replaced by a single Gradio panel with a mode selector, and
    model patching goes through forge_objects.unet rather than a cloned
    ComfyUI model object.

  * Added a Forge Neo code path. Forge Neo's pre-CFG hook fires before model
    evaluation, so the conditional and unconditional predictions are not
    available there; on that backend the extension registers a post-CFG hook
    instead and reconstructs the equivalent result. Where sd-webui-TCFG is
    active and ordered ahead of this extension, the post-CFG path reads the
    damped unconditional prediction TCFG stashes in model_options; otherwise
    it falls back to the raw unconditional prediction.

  * Added priority-based hook insertion. Forge-derived backends append
    pre-CFG hooks in registration order, which is effectively alphabetical
    and varies with the set of installed extensions. This extension inserts
    itself at priority 14.0 so that the assembled chain does not depend on
    what else happens to be present.

  * Added a chain dump, emitted at sampling time when the environment
    variable SD_WEBUI_SETI_DEBUG is set to 1, replacing the upstream nodes'
    ANSI-coloured startup prints.

  * Replaced the direct model_sampling.percent_to_sigma() calls with a helper
    that resolves the sigma schedule across the supported backends, reading
    unet.get_model_object("model_sampling") on reForge and Forge Classic and
    unet.model.predictor on Forge Neo. The percent boundaries are additionally
    short-circuited so that the default values never gate anything regardless
    of backend.

  * Converted the sigma argument to a Python float through a helper rather
    than indexing the tensor directly.

  * Did not port the upstream SkimFlipPreCFG (Timed Flip) and
    ConstantSkimPreCFG (Clean Skim) nodes as separate modes. Both are Single
    Scale with fixed parameter values, which the Single Scale controls
    already reproduce exactly; the equivalent settings are documented in
    README.md. Infotext written while these existed as modes is still read
    correctly and mapped back onto Single Scale.

  * Did not port the upstream DifferenceCFG_PreCFG node. It shares none of
    the skimming machinery in this module and lives in a separate extension,
    sd-webui-DifferenceCFG.

  * Added PNG infotext round-trip support using the "Skimmed CFG" key prefix,
    including the legacy-mode mapping described above, and XYZ Grid axes for
    the enabled flag and the mode selector.

  * Added exception handling around the hooks so that an internal failure
    returns the unmodified standard CFG output rather than aborting
    generation.
